## 3.4 ACTION BUTTONS - What They Actually Do

### 3.4.1 Primary Actions

**"Open all" button**
- **What it does:** Sets EVERY boundary pipe to OPEN (green)
- **When to use:** Starting point, want maximum connectivity, resetting to baseline
- **Effect on dashboard:** Open count = total boundaries

**"Close all (Boundaries)" button**
- **What it does:** Sets EVERY boundary pipe to CLOSED (red)
- **When to use:** Testing complete isolation, starting fresh for automatic selection
- **Effect on dashboard:** Open count = 0

### 3.4.2 Secondary Actions

**"⚡ Simulate" button**
- **What it does:** Runs EPANET hydraulic simulation with current boundary settings
- **What happens behind the scenes:**
  1. Takes current open/closed configuration
  2. Runs full hydraulic analysis
  3. Calculates flows, pressures, velocities, etc.
  4. Stores results in node_attributes and link_attributes
  5. Updates flow values for animation
  6. Populates tables and colormap data
- **When to click:** 
  - Immediately after loading (first thing you should do)
  - After any significant boundary changes
  - Before exporting data or creating reports
  - Before animation (animation needs flow data)
- **If simulation fails:** Falls back to random flows (still works for visualization)

**"▶️ Animate" button**
- **What it does:** Starts/stops flow animation on open boundaries
- **What you see:**
  - Gold dots appear on green (open) pipes
  - Dots move along pipe in flow direction
  - Speed is optimized for visibility
  - Dots wrap around (reach end, reappear at start)
  - Direction = positive flow (forward), negative flow (backward)
- **What happens when you click:**
  - First click: Animation starts
  - Second click: Animation stops, dots disappear
- **Important behavior:**
  - Animation automatically stops if you change boundaries
  - Zone polygons temporarily hide during animation (for clarity)
  - Only open boundaries show animation
  - Zero-flow pipes have stationary or no dots

**"💧 Show Boundary Flow Values" button**
- **What it does:** Toggles numeric flow labels on/off for open boundaries
- **What you see:**
  - White labels with black text appear at pipe midpoints
  - Format: "0.1234 m³/s" (units from your model)
  - Only appears on GREEN (open) boundaries
- **Click behavior:**
  - First click: Labels appear
  - Second click: Labels disappear
  - Button text toggles between "Show" and "Remove"
- **When to use:**
  - Need exact flow numbers for reporting
  - Want to compare flows visually
  - Before exporting data to verify values

**"💾 Save" button**
- **What it does:** Saves current boundary configuration and closes window
- **What gets saved:** Which pipes are open vs closed
- **What happens after:** Returns to main application with your settings
- **When to click:** You're done and want to keep your work

**"❌ Cancel" button**
- **What it does:** Closes window WITHOUT saving
- **What gets discarded:** All open/closed changes you made
- **When to click:** You changed your mind, made a mistake, want to start over

