2. Divides values into 5 equal ranges (quantiles)
3. Assigns color to each node based on its range
4. Displays colored nodes on map
5. Opens legend popup showing ranges

### 4.6.2 Color Scale

| Range | Color | Meaning |
|-------|-------|---------|
| 0-20% | Blue | Lowest values |
| 20-40% | Orange | Low-medium |
| 40-60% | Green | Medium |
| 60-80% | Red | High-medium |
| 80-100% | Purple | Highest values |

### 4.6.3 Legend Popup

When you apply colormap, a separate window appears showing:
- Attribute name
- Exact value ranges for each color
- Units of measurement

The popup:
- Positions itself to the right of main window
- Can be moved/resized
- Closing it removes the colormap

### 4.6.4 Interactive Colormap

If Interactive Mode is ON:
- Hover over colored nodes → popup shows exact value
- Great for identifying specific high/low points

### 4.6.5 When to Use

**Pressure colormap:** Spot low-pressure areas (blue) vs high-pressure (purple)
**Demand colormap:** Identify high-consumption nodes
**Elevation colormap:** Understand terrain effects
**Flow colormap:** See which nodes have high flow

### 4.6.6 Clearing Colormap

- Close the legend popup
- OR apply another colormap (replaces previous)
- OR click 🎨 again with different attribute

