# PART 5: INTERACTIVE MODE DEEP DIVE

## 5.1 Complete Description of Interactive Behavior

When you check "Interactive Links Mode," the application changes fundamentally.

### 5.1.1 Mouse Hover - Detailed

**What happens:**
1. Mouse position tracked continuously
2. Application calculates distance to every pipe midpoint
3. Finds closest pipe
4. If within threshold (2% of view width), highlights it YELLOW
5. Updates status bar with pipe information

**Status bar format:**
- For boundary pipes: "PipeName (Boundary) - Current Status - Value Units"
- For regular pipes: "PipeName - Value Units"
- If no attribute: just pipe name

**Visual feedback:**
- Yellow line appears (thicker than normal)
- Overrides any other coloring temporarily
- Disappears when mouse moves away

### 5.1.2 Mouse Click - Detailed

**Case 1: Click on GREEN boundary pipe**
1. Pipe status toggles to CLOSED
2. Color changes from green to red
3. Dashboard updates (open count decreases)
4. If "Hide closed boundaries" is checked, pipe disappears
5. Animation stops (if running)

**Case 2: Click on RED boundary pipe**
1. Pipe status toggles to OPEN
2. Color changes from red to green
3. Dashboard updates (open count increases)
4. If previously hidden, reappears
5. Animation stops (if running)

**Case 3: Click on DARK BLUE pipe (non-boundary)**
1. Popup dialog appears
2. Shows ALL available attributes for that pipe
3. Includes data from simulation if available
4. Useful for inspection without changes

**Case 4: Click on empty space**
- Nothing happens

### 5.1.3 Real-time Updates

Every click triggers:
- Dashboard statistics refresh
- Open count recalculates
- Zone pair counts update
- Redundancy indicator updates
- Visualization redraws if needed

---

## 5.2 Interactive Mode Strategies

### 5.2.1 Strategy: Progressive Isolation

**Goal:** Gradually reduce connections until reaching target

**Steps:**
1. Start with "Open all" (all green)
2. Check "Hide closed boundaries" (see only open)
3. Turn on Interactive Mode
4. Click green pipes one by one
5. Each click makes pipe disappear
6. Watch dashboard open count decrease
7. Stop when reaching desired number

**Advantage:** Visual focus on remaining open pipes only

### 5.2.2 Strategy: Selective Override

**Goal:** Keep automatic selection but override specific pipes

**Steps:**
1. Configure automatic selection (attributes, rules)
2. Let it apply (opens/closes pipes)
3. Turn on Interactive Mode
4. Click any pipe you disagree with to toggle it
5. Your manual changes persist
6. Can continue adjusting automatic settings later

**Advantage:** Best of both worlds - systematic plus manual fine-tuning

### 5.2.3 Strategy: Network Exploration

**Goal:** Learn your network

**Steps:**
1. Turn on Interactive Mode
2. Hover over pipes to identify them
3. Click non-boundary pipes to see their data
4. Use with colormap to see attribute distributions
5. Click table rows to locate elements

**Advantage:** No changes made, pure inspection

---

## 5.3 Interactive Mode Limitations

- Only boundary pipes can be toggled
- Clicks on regular pipes only show info
- Changes lost if not saved
- Animation resets when clicking
- Hover only works within view (not on hidden pipes)

