# PART 6: VISUALIZATION LAYERS MANAGEMENT

## 6.1 Complete Layer Reference

| Layer | Visual | Control | Default |
|-------|--------|---------|---------|
| Base network | Dark blue lines | Always on | Always on |
| Zone polygons | Colored blobs | "Show zone boundaries" | On |
| Open boundaries | Green thick lines | Automatic when boundaries exist | On |
| Closed boundaries | Red thick lines | "Hide closed boundaries" | On |
| Hover | Yellow thick line | Interactive Mode | Off |
| Filter highlight | Pink dashed | Filter menu | Off |
| Animation | Gold dots | "Animate" button | Off |
| Flow labels | White text boxes | "Show Flow Values" | Off |
| Colormap | Colored nodes | "Colormap" button | Off |
| Selection highlight | Yellow dot/label | Table row click | Off |

## 6.2 Layer Interactions

### 6.2.1 What Overrides What

When multiple layers compete for the same pipe:

**Priority order (highest to lowest):**
1. Hover (yellow) - temporary, overrides everything
2. Filter highlight (pink) - overrides boundary colors
3. Animation dots - appear on top of lines
4. Boundary colors (green/red) - normal state
5. Base network (dark blue) - default

### 6.2.2 What Hides What

**When "Hide closed boundaries" is ON:**
- Red pipes completely invisible
- They don't appear in hover detection
- They don't count for hover (can't hover what you can't see)

**When zone polygons are OFF:**
- Colored blobs disappear
- Zone boundaries still exist logically
- Zone labels also disappear

**During animation:**
- Zone polygons auto-hide (cleaner view)
- Returns when animation stops

### 6.2.3 Layer Combinations That Work Well

**Combination 1: Full analysis view**
- Base network
- Zone polygons (ON)
- Boundaries (both colors, show all)
- Flow labels (OFF)
- Animation (OFF)
- Colormap (OFF)

**Combination 2: Clean flow view**
- Base network
- Zone polygons (OFF)
- Boundaries (hide closed = ON)
- Animation (ON)
- Flow labels (OFF)
- Colormap (OFF)

**Combination 3: Data exploration**
- Base network
- Zone polygons (OFF)
- Boundaries (hide closed = ON or OFF as needed)
- Animation (OFF)
- Flow labels (ON)
- Colormap (ON)

**Combination 4: Element hunting**
- Base network
- Zone polygons (OFF)
- Boundaries (OFF via hide all? not possible)
- Filter highlight (ON)
- All others OFF

---

## 6.3 Layer Management Best Practices

### 6.3.1 Start Simple

Begin with only:
- Base network
- Zone polygons
- Boundaries (both colors)

Add layers only as needed.

### 6.3.2 One Dynamic Layer at a Time

Avoid having multiple moving/changing layers simultaneously:
- Don't run animation with flow labels (too cluttered)
- Don't run animation with colormap (competing attention)
- Don't use filter highlight with hover (pink vs yellow confusion)

### 6.3.3 Use "Hide Closed Boundaries" Strategically

- ON when you want to see only active connections
- OFF when you need to locate closed pipes
- Toggle back and forth to compare

### 6.3.4 Clear Filters When Done

Pink dashed lines persist until cleared. Use "Clear All Filters" when you're done with element hunting.

