# PART 18: GLOSSARY OF TERMS

| Term | Definition |
|------|------------|
| **Boundary pipe** | A pipe that connects two different zones OR connects a zone to unassigned area |
| **Open boundary** | A boundary pipe that allows flow (green) |
| **Closed boundary** | A boundary pipe that does NOT allow flow (red) |
| **Zone** | A user-defined area (pressure zone, DMA, etc.) drawn as polygon |
| **Zone pair** | Two zones that share at least one boundary pipe |
| **Node** | A point in the network (junction, reservoir, tank) |
| **Link** | A connection between nodes (pipe, pump, valve) |
| **Attribute** | A property of nodes or links (pressure, flow, diameter, etc.) |
| **Simulation** | Hydraulic calculation that determines flows and pressures |
| **Animation** | Moving dots showing flow direction on open boundaries |
| **Colormap** | Colored nodes showing attribute distribution |
| **Interactive Mode** | Mode where hovering and clicking on pipes works |
| **Quantile** | Equal-sized groups of data (used for colormap) |
| **Mask** | Internal representation of which pipes are boundaries/open |
| **Dashboard** | Top section of left panel showing statistics |

